<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard Format + interview, experiment and emails.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An organism with lilac orchid flora of which release spores that have corrosive and psychoactive properties. These spores can injure, cause a sudden conviction to &quot;save&quot; or conserve the plant thus increasing hunger and thirst in relation to the plant and causing auditory and visual hallucinations similar to that schizophrenia, mood swings characterized by a reaction similar to that of biological components and how plants communicate danger between organisms.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Plant arrives via a shipment quarantined in a port designated for general commercial shipping and shipping of parts for the local nuclear power plant, two incidents of the spores affecting small groups of people at the port and powerplant leading up to a meltdown in which the organism was recovered after radiation levels had subsided to a level acceptable for recovery efforts by foundation agents.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The psychoactive properties of the spore</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Shipped by unknown import/export company.</p>

