<p>I'll provide an explanation of incidents here and a brief discovery/history summary</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Incident 1- Port:<br />
- The organism arrives into the port under an unlisted shipping company, due to the biological nature of the shipment it is put into quarantine by a port worker. Within the next week a port worker exhibits the symptoms of psychoactive properties of the spores as well as a 2 other co-workers. Explained further via an interview from a police body to investigate the case's abnormality. Case is closed due to lack of evidence and organism is incinerated in line with port policy although it had grown outside the port due to mishandling.</p>
<p>Incident 2 - Nuclear Plant:<br />
- An increase in temperature in some of the reactors alerts personnel internally and a maintenance team is requested. Upon further inspection corrosion of the cooling system and growth of the vascular plant structure was noted. A maintenance worker affected by the spores inflicted self injury and displayed behaviour of warding other staff away from the plant, in this time the corrosive capabilities of the spores had corroded a major length of the cooling system leading to a reactor meltdown, however it is unknown how it went unnoticed by staff working nearby, presumed to be light exposure to the spores.</p>
<p>After history:<br />
The foundation recovers the organism after radiation levels subsided, MTF Theta 4 assists in the cleanup effort to minimize the effects and possible further release of spores.</p>
